From f9da73b725cf1e687794608bf455243aa4c2a99d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:15:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: panel brightness from CoreBrightness over DSI0

The brightness slider changed nothing: backboardd's CoreBrightness looks
for an AppleARMBacklight service with backlight-control and there was
none. AppleARMBacklight (published from AppleCLCD::start on umi) now has
IODisplayParameters, new-backlight-architecture, nits limits, a
marketing table and calibration parameters (DisplayCreateWithID gives
the display up without the table, and computes every slider position as
1 nit without the calibration). brightness-nits (nits x 65536) maps
linearly to the panel's DCS 0x51 level (2..0x7ff, 420 nits at the top,
at least 16), sent from a thread call through DSI0's command DMA as
Linux msm dsi_host.c does (buffer in the last cont_splash page: DMA_BASE
is 32 bits).

QuartzCore turns on libEDR once a backlight exists and then waited ~5 s
per frame on an EDR server that does not answer here, so backboardd's
single-service lookup does not see the backlight (sweetbl_hideca=0
shows it). Boot-args: sweetbl, sweetbl_maxnits, sweetbl_minlevel,
sweetbl_init, sweetbl_lp, sweetbl_buf, sweetbl_trace (property reads with
backboardd's user backtrace, sweet_user_bt_current in exception.c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
